{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487064423,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2MTAzNjI2MA=="},"added":["feedback-desired"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487064423,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2MTAzNjI2MQ=="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487065041,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1NjE3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279656172"},"message":"How exactly is `save_dataset` a problem? IIRC it explicitly does not care about \"untracked\" files. But staged and explicitly given path only. The reason why it is staged does not and should not matter here IMHO.\n\nAlso: `direct mode` is nothing that I would invest much in. We are debating here what happens when something is commited to a repo in mode that was invented for the purpose of making history and content modification as transparent as possible. I'd say: let it go ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487065312,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1NzI2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279657260"},"message":"It does not care for untracked files, yes. But it also tries to not care for unstaged changes. In order to do so, it is calling `dirty(index=True, working_tree=False, untracked_files=False)`, which is possible only, if we generally allow to use `working_tree` (or similar parameter).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487065445,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1Nzk2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279657964"},"message":"At this point of `save_dataset` we kind of want to stick to the concept of staged changes, while on the other hand we know, that this very concept isn't actually valid for annexes. I'm looking for a consistent way to approach this.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487065485,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1ODE3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279658172"},"message":"No, it sets that parameter because it wants to avoid the test. Remove it, and let it always avoid the test, and it will remain happy.\n\nEven with working_tree=True, it would not commit anything untracked, so the problem here has no consequences.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487065589,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1ODY5OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279658699"},"message":"A different approach would be to not test at all in `save_dataset`. The only reason it is doing the test in the present code is to avoid the spectacular fireworks should anyone dare to commit a change where there is none ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487066386,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY2MjAzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279662030"},"message":"Well, if this is the case, it never worked exactly as intended, I guess. ;-)\nBecause `working_true=False` does not just avoid the test, but gives a different result, if there are unstaged changes (which would be committed, if we change it to `with working_tree=True`.\n\nBut okay, if we actually care for untracked files only, we can just remove it, of course.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487066438,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY2MjIyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279662228"},"message":"Hah - would NOT be committed - commit() would fail instead, of course. Okay, got it. :-D","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487066937,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY2NDAzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279664034"},"message":"Worth reiterating: Often, the present approach of \"outside\" testing is the result of the behavior of the low-level layers to whine as hard and long as possible (e.g. #1111, ...). Many of these tests must be redundant, as either git-annex or git will do (some of) that again. Moving towards a result-based error behavior would avoid many issues like this and has the potential to speed things up, and make fewer bugs from fewer lines of code and fewer misinterpreted test conditions. I.e. If I tell the machine to save `fileX` and there is nothing to be saved, because there is no change, it is not an error, because the result is what I wanted -- all saved.\n\nI am not saying that it should not communicate back that it did nothing, but there is a difference between a litany of log ERRORs and `return False` or `return None`. Which would naturally go away, if we assumed that it is OK to call commit, even if there is a chance that there is nothing to commit.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487067187,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY2NDk5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279664998"},"message":"Yes, agree.\n\nOkay, so while `save_dataset` probably can just be called without `working_tree` (testing the approach right now), I'll keep this open, until the corresponding PR is done. Just in case I find more ...","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487067309,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50OTYxMTA1MDQ4"},"title":"we need a better concept than staged/unstaged (yet to be proven)","was":"we need a better concept than staged/unstaged (yet to be proven)"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487067354,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY2NTY3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-279665672"},"message":"I adjusted title and top-comment to document that there is no concrete evidence for a staged/unstaged problem yet.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536899073,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTIyNjk5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1289#issuecomment-421226996"},"message":"so no problem - no issue","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536899073,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTg0NTE3NjYyNA=="},"status":2}]}